\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The collapse law on 17 corpus and encoder pairs, sorted by the full out of sample $R^2$; the line separates the pairs that pass the diagnostic. $d$: TwoNN dimension, mean and sd over five pilots of 2{,}000 documents (and over three samples for the GTR forum corpora). $d$, ratio: the ratio of the $\log r$ and $\log n$ coefficients. $b$: exponent of Equation~\ref {eq:collapse} fitted on cells with $n \le 1{,}000$. $R^2$ pilot: fit on subsamples of one pilot with $n \le 750$, scored on $n$ from 1{,}000 to 2{,}000. $R^2$ full: fit on $n \le 1{,}000$, scored on $n$ up to 7{,}000. Errors: mean absolute error of the predicted $G$ at the largest $n$, for the collapse law and for a separate curve in $n$ at each radius.}}{6}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:collapse}{{1}{6}{The collapse law on 17 corpus and encoder pairs, sorted by the full out of sample $R^2$; the line separates the pairs that pass the diagnostic. $d$: TwoNN dimension, mean and sd over five pilots of 2{,}000 documents (and over three samples for the GTR forum corpora). $d$, ratio: the ratio of the $\log r$ and $\log n$ coefficients. $b$: exponent of Equation~\ref {eq:collapse} fitted on cells with $n \le 1{,}000$. $R^2$ pilot: fit on subsamples of one pilot with $n \le 750$, scored on $n$ from 1{,}000 to 2{,}000. $R^2$ full: fit on $n \le 1{,}000$, scored on $n$ up to 7{,}000. Errors: mean absolute error of the predicted $G$ at the largest $n$, for the collapse law and for a separate curve in $n$ at each radius}{table.caption.1}{}}
